Checking a table file with the Capla search
===========================================

htr3.b       the search of code/APaul/htr3_new.c for one line of a table, in
             Capla (gitlab.inria.fr/fresco/capla), with k, l and ERR as
             arguments: the table of differences, the window ERR on the top
             word of B_0, the walk j = 0 .. N-1.
main_htr3.c  C driver (Capla has no input/output): reads a table file in
             htr3_new.c's format, runs search on each line and prints the
             candidates x0 + j u, one per line, as htr3_new.c does.

Building.  Needs the Capla compiler in ~/git/capla-compiler (CAPLA=... to
change it), built in the opam switch capla:

  make          htr3cap: compiled by Capla's verified compiler (ccomp)
                htr3gcc: the same program written out as C by
                `ccomp -dcaplac` (unverified backend), then gcc -O2

Checking one file of the table.  The tables are in code/exptable9/archive,
five parts holding the 2203 files in<e>:

  mkdir tables
  for P in ../../../../exptable9/archive/tables*.tar.bz2; do
    tar xjf $P -C tables in1024 2>/dev/null; done
  ./htr3cap tables/in1024 9 6 0x600000 > in1024.htr

The loop takes in1024 from the part that holds it; without the file name
it unpacks all 2203 files.

The arguments are the file, k = 9, l = 6 and ERR = 0x600000 (hexadecimal),
the values of htr3_new.c.  The output lists every candidate of every line
of the file.  A line with more than 4000000 candidates stops the run.

Cost.  A line costs N steps (its second field).  Measured on the desktop
(one core, turbo off): 10^7 steps take 1.37 s with htr3cap, 1.13 s with
htr3gcc.  So a file costs the sum of its N column times 0.137 us:

  awk '{s += $2} END {print s * 0.137e-6 / 86400, "days"}' tables/in1024

  in1024    294 lines   6.1e12 steps   about 10 days      (scaled)
  in2       665 lines   4.5e15 steps   about 20 years     (scaled)
  archive               5.6e17 steps   about 2400 years   (scaled)

Test.  On the first line of in-1074 with N cut to 10^6, htr3cap, htr3gcc
and htr3_new.c print the same 3 candidates.

What is proved is in ../proof: on Capla's semantics, search returns every
j < N that the hypotheses of hscan_exp make hard to round.  The C driver
(reading, frexp, x0 + j u, printing) is not proved.
